<section class="private" id="private">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">private sessions</div>
    <h2>private sessions</h2>
    <p>one-on-one practice tailored to your body, experience, and what you want to explore in your practice.</p>
    <p>whether you are building a foundation, refining your practice, or working towards something specific, each session is shaped around you.</p>
    <p>available online or in person, depending on location.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn light" href="https://cal.com/luna-namaskar/private-yoga-session" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-book="private-yoga-session">book a private class with me</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section teacher" id="teacher">
  <div class="teacher-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow">bio</div>
    <h2>the teacher</h2>
    <p>regine blanco is a yoga teacher from the philippines with years of practice, study, and teaching across asia. after completing her training in rishikesh, india, she continued teaching in indonesia, including at studios such as samadi and moana nuanu.</p>
    <p>her classes combine clear technique with an emphasis on breath and body awareness. the goal is not to perform asanas, but to use them as a way to gain a practical understanding of the body and, ultimately, of yourself.</p>
    <p>her teaching is rooted in traditional yogic philosophy, while making the practice accessible, engaging, and relevant to modern practitioners.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bio-photo"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64, " alt="Regine Blanco practicing yoga"><div class="caption">Luna Namaskar · Practice in movement</div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="styles">
  <div class="practice-intro">
    <h2>find your practice</h2>
    <div class="note">different practices, different intentions. explore what feels right for you.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="styles">
    <div class="style"><h3>vinyasa flow</h3><p>dynamic, fluid movement guided by the breath. energizing, strengthening, and focused.</p></div>
    <div class="style"><h3>hatha</h3><p>a slower, grounded practice with time to understand how your body relates to each posture. includes breath awareness and pranayama.</p></div>
    <div class="style"><h3>yin</h3><p>longer-held postures and stillness to encourage release, mobility, and a quieter mind.</p></div>
    <div class="style"><h3>yin yang</h3><p>a balance of dynamic movement and stillness, combining the energy of vinyasa with the deeper release of yin.</p></div>
    <div class="style"><h3>power yoga</h3><p>a strong, dynamic practice designed to build heat, strength, stability, and mental focus.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

